  | Info | /Users/vbb/IdeaProjects/creditsAI/frontend/src/app/core/auth/auth.config.spec.ts:52-58 | Test gaps in the negative cases. `//evil.example.com/api/clients` (protocol-relative) is not tested. It is correctly rejected because the regex is anchored on `^/api`, but it is the classic bypass and deserves a test. Two more inputs are worth pinning: `/API/clients` (not matched because the regex has no `i` flag; that fails safe) and `http://localhost/api/clients` (absolute same-origin, also not matched, so a future service that builds absolute URLs would silently get 401s rather than leak). | Add `//evil.example.com/api/clients`, `/API/clients` and `http://localhost/api/clients` to the "should not attach" list, so the anchoring can't regress. |
