  ## Tika artifacts and the OOXML deviation
  - **Only `org.apache.tika:tika-core:3.3.3`** (new `tika.version` property in `pom.xml`).
  - **What tika-core can and cannot detect.** It identifies PDF, ODT (via its `mimetype` entry), TXT, JPEG, PNG, GIF, WEBP, HEIC and TIFF from magic bytes. It reports DOCX and XLSX only as a generic `application/zip`. I confirmed this with real tests that failed.
  - **Why not the Tika OOXML detector.** It lives in `tika-parser-microsoft-module`, which pulls in POI, jackcess, BouncyCastle and html/xml/text parsers. `tika-parser-zip-commons` does not help; I tried it and removed it.
  - **My workaround.** `storage/OoxmlInspector` uses only the JDK. For a zip result it reads `[Content_Types].xml` (max 256 KB, StAX with DTD/external entities disabled). It accepts DOCX only if `/word/document.xml` is declared with the Word main content type and the part exists, and XLSX likewise for `/xl/workbook.xml`. Macro and template variants and plain zips are rejected.
  - **Your call:** if you want pure Tika, swap in `tika-parser-microsoft-module` (heavy). Otherwise keep this.
  - The file name is never passed to Tika, so the extension cannot influence detection.
  
